  "tips": [
    {
      "id": "phone",
      "title": "On the phone",
      "text": "In France you pick up the phone and say « Allô ? ». You use allô only on the phone. Then you say who you are: « C'est Viv. »"
    },
    {
      "id": "manif",
      "title": "Une manif",
      "text": "When French people want something changed, they often walk down the street together with signs and songs. This is une manifestation, or une manif for short, and the traffic has to wait."
    },
    {
      "id": "bus",
      "title": "Getting about Paris",
      "text": "Paris has buses, a métro under the streets, and bikes you can hire from racks on the pavement. Many people in Paris have no car at all."
    }
  ],
